This is the optimal two-pointer approach and correctly computes trapped water for inputs whose result fits in an int.

## Approach
- The solution maintains leftMax and rightMax while moving two pointers inward. 
- When height[left] <= height[right], the left side is the limiting barrier, so the left position can be finalized using leftMax;
-  otherwise, the right position is finalized using rightMax. Each position is processed once, and the logic matches the optimal two-pointer solution.

## Solution
```java[]
class Solution {
    public int trap(int[] height) {
        int left=0;
        int  right=height.length-1;
        int leftMax=0;
        int rightMax=0;
        int total=0;

        while(left<=right){
            if(height[left]<=height[right]){
                if(height[left]>=leftMax){
                    leftMax=height[left];
                }
                else{
                    total+=leftMax-height[left];
                }
                left++;
            }
            else{
                if(height[right]>=rightMax){
                    rightMax=height[right];
                }
                else{
                    total+=rightMax-height[right];
                }
                right--;
            }
        }
        return total;
    }
}
```

